## How to use this template

1. Copy to `~/.claude/agents/<project>-orchestrator.md`
2. Replace placeholders:
   - `<project>` — the project name
   - `<key technologies>` — stack summary for initialPrompt
   - `<key conventions>` — project-specific rules
3. Confirm referenced subagents exist (`@feature-planner`, `@test-verifier`, etc.)
4. Start a session: `claude --agent <project>-orchestrator`
5. Test the workflow on a small feature first

## When to use this template

Only worthwhile when:
- You work on `<project>` repeatedly (the orchestrator's initialPrompt amortizes over many sessions)
- Workflow is stable (planner → implement → verify is consistent)
- Team / future-you benefits from a documented entry point

For one-off projects or constantly-changing workflows — don't bother. Just invoke agents directly from main as needed.
